NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - THE BAND: the papers' noise boundary is the average absolute move from the open at that minute over the last 14 days; the family's band is fixed for the day at k x the daily ATR(14) (Conti's form).
  - THE EXIT: the papers exit on a VWAP / boundary trailing stop or at the close; the engine runs the fixed 40 / 60 point bracket instead.
  - THE GRID: the papers decide every 30 minutes; here every 15-minute close.
  - STATE, NOT EVENT: at the first close of the mid and pm passes (11:15, 13:45) a price that is already beyond the band enters at once (the papers' rule is a state too).
  - THE CAP IS PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 1 counts inside each of the 3 passes, so a day can hold up to 3 trades; the passes are independent instances, so a trade of one pass may still be open when the next pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only; the hunt's stack step applies one-at-a-time across legs).
  - THE FAMILY'S MONTHS: the globex-anchored long-only noise sheets had unseen reads and a block walk-forward (nq_noise_gx_mid_long): this sheet's anchor, sides and bar differ, but the family's test months are partly seen.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, $4 a round turn, tick replay, 1 NQ).
  - FLAT: every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30); the 3:1 block walk-forward is a separate, pre-registered read (hunt PREREG Gate 2).

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - CAPPED PER SESSION PASS, NOT PER DAY: max_trades 1 counts inside each pass (3 passes: nyam, mid, pm), so a day can hold up to 3 trades; a family's own loss or trade count (none) counts inside one pass too.
  - The passes are independent: a trade of one pass may still be open when another pass enters (one position at a time holds inside a pass only).
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
